WEBVTT

00:00:45.546 --> 00:00:48.799
<i>Kokoro egakidasu</i>

00:00:48.799 --> 00:00:52.386
<i>chizujou no michinaru frontier</i>

00:00:52.386 --> 00:00:55.806
<i>Tobira hiraitara</i>

00:00:55.806 --> 00:00:59.142
<i>michi wa tsuzuiteiru yo</i>

00:00:59.142 --> 00:01:05.107
<i>Hokori makiagete kimi no machi e</i>

00:01:05.107 --> 00:01:11.822
<i>Sora to daichi ga kasanaru ruuto de</i>

00:01:11.822 --> 00:01:15.576
<i>Hashiru minamikaze ni notte</i>

00:01:15.576 --> 00:01:18.495
<i>Aoku somaru kaze wo kitte</i>

00:01:18.495 --> 00:01:25.627
<i>Kokorogoto kakedashiteirun da</i>

00:01:25.627 --> 00:01:29.131
<i>Mahiru no tsuki wo oikoshite</i>

00:01:29.131 --> 00:01:32.259
<i>Kinou to wa chigau sekai e</i>

00:01:32.259 --> 00:01:37.681
<i>Dokomademo hashirinuketeku</i>

00:01:37.681 --> 00:01:41.602
<i>Ano kaze no you ni</i>

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:46.899
<i>Ano kaze no you ni</i>

00:02:04.458 --> 00:02:06.585
To repeat:

00:02:06.585 --> 00:02:09.671
In a press conference just held,
the Beijing government has announced

00:02:09.671 --> 00:02:12.382
that if there are no signs
of a resolution by 6:00,

00:02:12.382 --> 00:02:16.887
the situation will inevitably
develop into a serious crisis.

00:02:16.887 --> 00:02:20.557
In response, Secretary-General Chang
of South China,

00:02:20.557 --> 00:02:21.892
also known as the
Democratic Federation of China,

00:02:21.892 --> 00:02:23.435
questioned if there was some connection

00:02:23.435 --> 00:02:26.355
to the terrorist acts committed
by the unidentified AS...

00:02:26.355 --> 00:02:27.856
Listen up.

00:02:27.856 --> 00:02:31.610
"Burning Hong Kong"
We have until 6:00 AM, which means we have 90 minutes left.

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:33.487
"Burning Hong Kong"
If we fail, that's it.

00:02:33.487 --> 00:02:36.406
Hong Kong will become a sea of flames.

00:02:36.406 --> 00:02:39.034
And I doubt it will stop there.

00:02:41.245 --> 00:02:43.956
You kept her face pretty?

00:02:43.956 --> 00:02:46.250
Apparently you're soft on women.

00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:49.127
Haven't you found Yu Fang yet?

00:02:49.127 --> 00:02:53.382
All of the preparations are complete.
Just watch.

00:02:57.177 --> 00:03:00.889
Big Sis, this is Yu Lan!

00:03:00.889 --> 00:03:04.518
I'm surrounded by all these scary men!

00:03:04.518 --> 00:03:06.436
What are you doing?

00:03:06.436 --> 00:03:08.021
No! Let me go!

00:03:08.021 --> 00:03:10.774
Oh no, I've been caught!

00:03:10.774 --> 00:03:13.819
Help me, Big Sis!

00:03:13.819 --> 00:03:15.529
Ow! Ow!

00:03:15.529 --> 00:03:16.446
I'm gonna die!

00:03:16.446 --> 00:03:18.448
No more! Not there!

00:03:23.245 --> 00:03:28.292
This is a situation neither
the North nor the South should want.

00:03:28.292 --> 00:03:29.459
Not only that,

00:03:29.459 --> 00:03:32.921
there's absolutely no consistency
to the Venom's destruction.

00:03:32.921 --> 00:03:35.632
So it's most likely the work
of someone operating independently.

00:03:35.632 --> 00:03:39.469
But who in the world would make
the North and South fight each other,

00:03:39.469 --> 00:03:42.848
and for what purpose?

00:03:45.809 --> 00:03:47.895
President Hunter, you have a guest.

00:03:47.895 --> 00:03:51.356
She has been anxious to see you.
It seems urgent.

00:03:51.356 --> 00:03:52.983
Turn her away.

00:03:52.983 --> 00:03:55.777
Even you should understand
what kind of crisis I'm facing right now.

00:03:55.777 --> 00:03:56.862
Hey! Get out of my way!

00:03:56.862 --> 00:03:58.614
Hey you, you shouldn't be here!

00:03:58.614 --> 00:04:01.116
I'm telling you to let me see him!

00:04:01.116 --> 00:04:03.035
A Helmajistani?

00:04:03.035 --> 00:04:04.995
Nope, don't know anyone like that.

00:04:04.995 --> 00:04:10.751
But a lot of Arabs live
in that building over there.

00:04:15.589 --> 00:04:17.758
So you're Kashim, huh?

00:04:17.758 --> 00:04:20.761
You reek of alcohol, you worthless brat.

00:04:20.761 --> 00:04:23.764
Are you trying to ruin the
reputation of "Bdakshon's Tiger"?

00:04:23.764 --> 00:04:26.892
As if I even care. State your business.

00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:32.689
A Chinese girl asked me
to give this to you.

00:04:32.689 --> 00:04:34.775
Take it and get lost.

00:05:06.723 --> 00:05:09.560
Five possible sniping positions.

00:05:35.419 --> 00:05:37.546
Sousuke Sagara, correct?

00:05:37.546 --> 00:05:38.630
Correct.

00:05:38.630 --> 00:05:42.718
There is a taxi waiting at
the north exit of the park. Get in it.

00:05:47.347 --> 00:05:48.724
Who asked you to do this?

00:05:48.724 --> 00:05:52.936
Does this have some connection
to the incidents occurring here?

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:10.621
State your name.

00:06:10.621 --> 00:06:12.789
What would you do if I told you?

00:06:14.708 --> 00:06:20.964
Sousuke Sagara. Go to the second floor
of the building behind you.

00:06:20.964 --> 00:06:25.469
<i>He </i>is waiting for you
in the back room there.

00:06:25.469 --> 00:06:26.803
Who is "he"?

00:06:26.803 --> 00:06:30.766
I suggest you try to remember
what this place is called.

00:06:39.650 --> 00:06:41.818
Kowloon?

00:07:33.662 --> 00:07:34.830
Yo!

00:07:34.830 --> 00:07:36.957
What has it been, three months?

00:07:36.957 --> 00:07:40.419
I'm so glad to see you, Kashim.

00:07:40.419 --> 00:07:42.921
Ga-Gauron!

00:07:42.921 --> 00:07:45.799
You seem so completely shocked.

00:07:45.799 --> 00:07:49.303
Is it really that strange
that I'm still alive?

00:07:49.303 --> 00:07:51.722
Back then... You should've...

00:07:51.722 --> 00:07:53.891
<i>Died</i>, is that it?

00:07:53.891 --> 00:07:55.851
I sure hope you haven't forgotten, now.

00:07:55.851 --> 00:08:00.981
My Codarl was equipped
with a Lambda Driver, you know.

00:08:00.981 --> 00:08:05.068
It can even protect the operator
when the unit self-destructs.

00:08:05.068 --> 00:08:08.238
Well, I still ended up like this anyway.

00:08:09.489 --> 00:08:13.577
Hey, now. Just look at
the kind of condition I'm in.

00:08:13.577 --> 00:08:16.872
I think it's pointless to be hasty.

00:08:16.872 --> 00:08:18.832
What is it you're after?

00:08:18.832 --> 00:08:22.794
Come on, now.
I just wanted to chat with you.

00:08:22.794 --> 00:08:23.962
Stop playing with me!

00:08:23.962 --> 00:08:25.839
But I'm serious.

00:08:28.467 --> 00:08:31.929
As you can see, my time is running out.

00:08:31.929 --> 00:08:38.769
So I had the Codarl go berserk through
the city, to lure you and that white AS here.

00:08:38.769 --> 00:08:43.190
And I scattered messages
to you all over the city.

00:08:43.190 --> 00:08:45.567
Majid was a tactician
who once made a name for himself

00:08:45.567 --> 00:08:48.612
as a guerilla leader in Helmajistan.

00:08:48.612 --> 00:08:51.114
His nickname was "Bdakshon's Tiger."

00:08:51.114 --> 00:08:54.618
And then there's the assassin
he gave a name to: Kashim.

00:08:54.618 --> 00:08:59.665
In other words, "The son
of Bdakshon's Tiger" is you.

00:08:59.665 --> 00:09:02.835
Hamidra is a former electrician
and a comrade of yours.

00:09:02.835 --> 00:09:06.171
I knew that if I sent out a message to
"Meet Hamidra at Tsim Sha Tsui,"

00:09:06.171 --> 00:09:10.884
you'd track down a
Helmajistani electrician.

00:09:10.884 --> 00:09:15.973
It was a message that would get through
to no one else in the world but you.

00:09:15.973 --> 00:09:20.769
But I thought you would bring
a bunch of your friends with you.

00:09:20.769 --> 00:09:22.646
Why did you come by yourself?

00:09:22.646 --> 00:09:24.731
Did something happen?

00:09:24.731 --> 00:09:26.608
That's none of your business!

00:09:27.609 --> 00:09:30.988
So you've finally started
to feel uncomfortable, huh?

00:09:30.988 --> 00:09:32.197
What?

00:09:32.197 --> 00:09:34.449
In Mithril, I mean.

00:09:34.449 --> 00:09:37.953
Being in a military unit that has
pretensions of being an ally of Justice

00:09:37.953 --> 00:09:40.205
is enough to frustrate anybody.

00:09:40.205 --> 00:09:43.166
Especially a man like you.

00:09:48.338 --> 00:09:50.382
Are you through with your speech?

00:09:50.382 --> 00:09:54.052
Then tell me about the
organization behind you.

00:09:55.762 --> 00:10:00.475
I'm amazed. Your work is
still that important to you?

00:10:01.018 --> 00:10:04.688
Fine then. I'll tell you.

00:10:04.688 --> 00:10:06.648
Amalgam.

00:10:06.648 --> 00:10:09.693
That's the name of
the organization I was working for.

00:10:09.693 --> 00:10:12.905
Its goals are the research and
development of the latest weapons,

00:10:12.905 --> 00:10:14.948
and the testing of them in actual combat.

00:10:14.948 --> 00:10:18.243
They would even create
regional conflicts to do so.

00:10:18.243 --> 00:10:19.745
A large number of Amalgam sympathizers

00:10:19.745 --> 00:10:23.624
have permeated the
hard-line factions of every nation.

00:10:23.624 --> 00:10:26.835
There are a lot of guys in both the East
and West who want to create a Cold War,

00:10:26.835 --> 00:10:30.506
and maintain a demand for munitions.

00:10:30.506 --> 00:10:33.759
Is that organization involved
in the turmoil here, too?

00:10:33.759 --> 00:10:36.512
No, this is my own handiwork.

00:10:36.512 --> 00:10:42.518
I'll bet those Amalgam guys are going
crazy trying to find us right about now.

00:10:44.937 --> 00:10:46.605
Venom!

00:10:46.605 --> 00:10:47.689
Yu Fang?

00:10:47.689 --> 00:10:49.650
It is time for me to go.

00:10:49.650 --> 00:10:52.402
I see. Take care.

00:10:52.402 --> 00:10:55.030
Farewell, Sensei.

00:10:59.576 --> 00:11:05.499
A long time ago, I raised a set
of twins named Yu Fang and Yu Lan.

00:11:05.499 --> 00:11:10.796
They were a lot like you.
Even now they're still as loyal as dogs.

00:11:10.796 --> 00:11:15.133
The turmoil here happened
because I ordered them to cause it.

00:11:15.133 --> 00:11:20.013
But tonight, Yu Fang is probably
going to die fighting Mithril.

00:11:20.013 --> 00:11:24.101
And if they don't get her, she'll just
get killed by Amalgam's Task Force.

00:11:24.101 --> 00:11:25.894
Task Force?

00:11:25.894 --> 00:11:28.105
They're a terrifying bunch.

00:11:28.105 --> 00:11:30.774
The commander of that task force
is incredibly skilled,

00:11:30.774 --> 00:11:32.401
but one hell of a nutcase.

00:11:32.401 --> 00:11:35.445
Your friends probably don't
stand a chance against him.

00:11:35.445 --> 00:11:39.032
The moment they run into him,
they'll all be killed.

00:11:39.032 --> 00:11:41.702
She's appeared! She's in Jordan!

00:11:41.702 --> 00:11:46.039
All right! Time to hunt
the little kitty down!

00:11:46.039 --> 00:11:48.917
You said "Amalgam," right?

00:11:48.917 --> 00:11:51.879
Are there any Whispered
in that organization?

00:11:51.879 --> 00:11:55.340
Yes. He is becoming
one of the key members.

00:11:55.340 --> 00:11:58.760
If they have a Whispered,
then why are they targeting Chidori?

00:11:58.760 --> 00:12:00.470
They shouldn't need her anymore, right?

00:12:00.470 --> 00:12:02.806
Because it's not complete.

00:12:02.806 --> 00:12:05.267
Apparently there are
differences in the knowledge

00:12:05.267 --> 00:12:08.353
that each individual Whispered has.

00:12:08.353 --> 00:12:10.105
If there's someone
who has extensive knowledge

00:12:10.105 --> 00:12:11.899
of the theory behind
Lambda Driver technology,

00:12:11.899 --> 00:12:16.653
there's also someone who only has
knowledge of submarine technology.

00:12:16.653 --> 00:12:19.907
That's why every time
a new Whispered is found,

00:12:19.907 --> 00:12:24.036
it's necessary to determine
which field that one is strong in.

00:12:24.036 --> 00:12:25.287
That's what those tests that we ran

00:12:25.287 --> 00:12:27.831
on that girl in the
Khanka Autonomous Region were for.

00:12:27.831 --> 00:12:32.961
And the results showed that
Kaname Chidori is a Whispered.

00:12:32.961 --> 00:12:36.798
That's all I've heard, though.

00:12:36.798 --> 00:12:38.634
Where is Amalgam's base?!

00:12:38.634 --> 00:12:40.761
Who are their key figures?

00:12:40.761 --> 00:12:44.431
Gimme a break already.
I'm getting sick of this subject.

00:12:44.431 --> 00:12:48.393
It's boring, and it's not
even the main issue here.

00:12:48.393 --> 00:12:52.523
Hey now, does it look
like I care if I die?

00:12:56.777 --> 00:12:59.905
Tell me. Please.

00:12:59.905 --> 00:13:05.035
"Please," huh? Are you really
the same Kashim I knew?

00:13:05.035 --> 00:13:06.245
What?

00:13:06.245 --> 00:13:08.038
Remember!

00:13:08.038 --> 00:13:13.418
What were you doing when
I first met you five years ago?

00:13:13.418 --> 00:13:16.296
Back then, I was an instructor
at a mercenary camp.

00:13:16.296 --> 00:13:19.383
You were a guerilla fighting
against the Soviets.

00:13:19.383 --> 00:13:23.804
We weren't allies, but we
weren't really enemies either.

00:13:23.804 --> 00:13:26.598
I still remember it<i> very </i>well.

00:13:26.598 --> 00:13:30.060
You had a really good look
in your eyes back then.

00:13:30.060 --> 00:13:32.729
Eyes that didn't either reject or affirm life.

00:13:32.729 --> 00:13:36.066
Eyes without any worries, doubts, or suffering.

00:13:36.066 --> 00:13:40.070
Yes, eyes like those of a saint.

00:13:40.070 --> 00:13:44.825
Anyone would probably
say they were beautiful.

00:13:44.825 --> 00:13:46.159
Do you understand?

00:13:46.159 --> 00:13:50.038
In other words, there was consistency,
no contradiction.

00:13:50.038 --> 00:13:55.502
When we met again in Khanka, your eyes
were still as beautiful as I remembered.

00:13:55.502 --> 00:13:59.047
The eyes of someone
who has no human weakness.

00:13:59.047 --> 00:14:01.091
I thought it would've been pretty nice

00:14:01.091 --> 00:14:05.179
if I could've killed you
the way you were then.

00:14:05.179 --> 00:14:07.055
But that...

00:14:07.055 --> 00:14:09.099
What's with that face?

00:14:12.728 --> 00:14:15.814
Venom spotted! It's in the Jordan area.

00:14:15.814 --> 00:14:20.194
Equip the ARX-7 with
a rapid-deployment booster.

00:14:20.194 --> 00:14:22.112
Supply it with a Boxer shot cannon,

00:14:22.112 --> 00:14:24.072
and put it on standby in the elevator.

00:14:24.072 --> 00:14:28.285
Captain, the use of the Arbalest
is supposed to be prohibited.

00:14:28.285 --> 00:14:30.120
We can use it as a decoy.

00:14:30.120 --> 00:14:33.165
I want to reduce the danger
they are in as much as I can.

00:14:33.165 --> 00:14:36.335
And besides, Sagara still hasn't...

00:14:36.335 --> 00:14:38.295
I am sorry to say this, Captain,

00:14:38.295 --> 00:14:42.174
but the only conclusion I can come to is
that Sagara has abandoned his mission.

00:14:42.174 --> 00:14:46.220
Relying on that AS and
that man is an obvious mistake.

00:14:46.220 --> 00:14:48.305
You cannot say that for certain.

00:14:49.014 --> 00:14:51.808
This is not some school club activity!

00:14:51.808 --> 00:14:52.809
I am well aware of that!

00:14:52.809 --> 00:14:54.937
Are you going to lecture me
<i>now </i>of all times?

00:14:54.937 --> 00:14:58.065
Ma'am, this time I simply
refuse to stand by and watch!

00:14:58.065 --> 00:14:59.608
You are allowing your
personal feelings to interfere,

00:14:59.608 --> 00:15:02.903
and are even trying to twist
an order from the highest level!

00:15:02.903 --> 00:15:05.155
What will become of the
organization and its regulations?

00:15:05.155 --> 00:15:06.198
Not only that,

00:15:06.198 --> 00:15:09.493
you are giving preferential treatment
to an officer who has abandoned his duty.

00:15:09.493 --> 00:15:10.744
This is outrageous!

00:15:10.744 --> 00:15:11.745
Very well.

00:15:11.745 --> 00:15:13.205
Then tell me,

00:15:13.205 --> 00:15:17.000
who was it who forced a ridiculous amount
of heavy responsibility upon that officer?

00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:19.044
Well, uh...

00:15:19.044 --> 00:15:23.048
It was<i> us</i>! If you think otherwise,
then tell me!

00:15:23.048 --> 00:15:25.342
Six months ago at that airport,

00:15:25.342 --> 00:15:29.012
who was it who risked his own life in order
to provide us with valuable information?

00:15:29.012 --> 00:15:34.184
Four months ago, who was it who faced
an absurdly powerful enemy machine

00:15:34.184 --> 00:15:36.478
without any preparation and defeated it?

00:15:36.478 --> 00:15:38.063
Deep in the mountains of Helmajistan,

00:15:38.063 --> 00:15:40.232
who was it who recaptured a
nuclear warhead that was being smuggled

00:15:40.232 --> 00:15:44.444
even while his comrades were
being killed one by one?

00:15:44.444 --> 00:15:48.949
Three months ago, who was it
who gave his all to protect this ship?

00:15:48.949 --> 00:15:51.994
Tell me, who was it?

00:15:51.994 --> 00:15:54.037
It was Sergeant Sagara.

00:15:54.037 --> 00:15:54.830
Correct.

00:15:54.830 --> 00:15:57.165
And yet you're still going to blame him?

00:15:57.165 --> 00:16:01.086
You're going to just brand him a coward?

00:16:01.086 --> 00:16:02.421
No.

00:16:03.755 --> 00:16:06.008
If you really want me to, I'll admit it.

00:16:06.008 --> 00:16:08.135
I love him.

00:16:08.135 --> 00:16:10.762
But those personal feelings
are irrelevant right now.

00:16:10.762 --> 00:16:13.348
I am positive he will return and do his job.

00:16:13.348 --> 00:16:15.517
He will not abandon us.

00:16:15.517 --> 00:16:17.352
No matter how hopeless
he may seem right now,

00:16:17.352 --> 00:16:21.023
I am sure he will pull himself
together again and come back to us.

00:16:21.023 --> 00:16:23.567
You can't change a person's basic nature.

00:16:23.567 --> 00:16:26.904
So he will come back,
because he is strong and kind!

00:16:26.904 --> 00:16:29.406
Strong and kind?

00:16:29.406 --> 00:16:32.784
Captain, do you think that
is enough to convince me?

00:16:32.784 --> 00:16:35.037
It's not about that, is it?

00:16:35.037 --> 00:16:39.917
What you doubt is my judgment.

00:16:39.917 --> 00:16:46.048
Commander Richard Mardukas.
Do you believe in me? Or do you not?

00:16:46.048 --> 00:16:47.674
Are you going to believe in me,
Teletha Testarossa,

00:16:47.674 --> 00:16:51.512
who has protected this ship to this day?

00:16:51.512 --> 00:16:54.556
Go on, make your decision.

00:17:05.108 --> 00:17:07.861
You've grown strong, haven't you?

00:17:10.364 --> 00:17:11.698
Aye, ma'am!

00:17:11.698 --> 00:17:15.410
Equip the ARX-7 with
a rapid deployment booster

00:17:15.410 --> 00:17:18.247
and Boxer shot cannon,

00:17:18.247 --> 00:17:20.082
and have it stand by in the elevator!

00:17:20.082 --> 00:17:23.418
Equip the ARX-7 with
a rapid deployment booster

00:17:23.418 --> 00:17:25.462
and Boxer shot cannon,

00:17:25.462 --> 00:17:28.799
and have it stand by in the elevator. Aye.

00:17:28.799 --> 00:17:30.467
Thank you.

00:17:30.467 --> 00:17:34.638
I want everyone to make it back safely!

00:17:34.638 --> 00:17:36.265
She says...

00:17:36.265 --> 00:17:38.308
The communication line
just opened on its own.

00:17:38.308 --> 00:17:41.019
Did someone let us hear that on purpose?

00:17:41.019 --> 00:17:42.020
Who knows.

00:17:42.020 --> 00:17:46.984
But I never would've expected Tessa to
argue so forcefully with the XO like that.

00:17:46.984 --> 00:17:49.778
She wants everyone to
make it back safely, huh?

00:17:49.778 --> 00:17:51.446
What do you think, guys?

00:17:51.446 --> 00:17:53.156
That's what I intend to do, of course.

00:17:53.156 --> 00:17:57.286
We can't make our princess sad,
now can we?

00:17:57.286 --> 00:18:01.957
To think she'd be so worried
about us... I'm honestly moved!

00:18:01.957 --> 00:18:03.458
It's just like her.

00:18:03.458 --> 00:18:05.210
She's a good officer.

00:18:05.210 --> 00:18:07.796
We have until 0600 hours.

00:18:07.796 --> 00:18:09.673
If you call yourselves pros,
you'd better live up to that.

00:18:09.673 --> 00:18:12.843
I don't make mistakes.
You don't make mistakes, either.

00:18:12.843 --> 00:18:14.636
And that's going to get everything
wrapped up nice and tight.

00:18:14.636 --> 00:18:15.721
Got that?

00:18:15.721 --> 00:18:17.181
--Roger!
--Roger!

00:18:48.337 --> 00:18:49.963
What a horrible look
you've got on your face.

00:18:49.963 --> 00:18:53.383
Are you worried? Or maybe torn?

00:18:53.383 --> 00:18:56.512
What happened to the "saint" I knew?

00:18:56.512 --> 00:18:58.013
I'm disappointed.

00:18:58.013 --> 00:19:01.725
You're full of internal conflict now.
You're not even worth killing.

00:19:01.725 --> 00:19:02.851
Shut up!

00:19:02.851 --> 00:19:08.232
You're the same as me. So why are you
trying to be a normal guy now?

00:19:08.232 --> 00:19:09.274
You make me want to puke.

00:19:09.274 --> 00:19:10.442
I'm telling you to shut up!

00:19:10.442 --> 00:19:12.694
No, I'm telling<i> you</i>.

00:19:12.694 --> 00:19:15.656
Ever since you met those guys
at Mithril and at that school,

00:19:15.656 --> 00:19:17.282
you've become worthless.

00:19:17.282 --> 00:19:21.995
You've gotten pulled in by those
worthless scum and become a bore.

00:19:21.995 --> 00:19:25.415
I just told you a little while ago
that you were frustrated, right?

00:19:25.415 --> 00:19:30.170
That's their fault.
Their so-called "humanism."

00:19:30.170 --> 00:19:33.549
The assassin-saint Kashim
I knew would never fit in there.

00:19:33.549 --> 00:19:36.510
You're being suckered by them.

00:19:36.510 --> 00:19:40.556
Listen. The weak are
parasites of the strong.

00:19:40.556 --> 00:19:43.767
They dazzle you with words
like "kind friend" and "trust,"

00:19:43.767 --> 00:19:48.188
and then they suck your strength
until there's nothing left.

00:19:48.188 --> 00:19:49.857
Tell me your<i> true </i>feelings.

00:19:49.857 --> 00:19:53.235
Do you really enjoy being
with a bunch of weaklings?

00:19:53.235 --> 00:19:55.237
Come on, answer me.

00:19:55.237 --> 00:19:58.615
I'm asking you if you really enjoy
being with a bunch of weaklings.

00:19:58.615 --> 00:19:59.366
Well?

00:19:59.366 --> 00:20:01.493
I'm telling you to shut the hell up!

00:20:04.329 --> 00:20:07.499
So you don't even have
the drive to kill me?

00:20:09.877 --> 00:20:12.004
I'm going to die soon.

00:20:12.004 --> 00:20:16.133
And I plan on bringing
others down with me.

00:20:16.133 --> 00:20:18.886
I ordered Yu Fang to
go berserk in Hong Kong

00:20:18.886 --> 00:20:22.306
until the whole city is a sea of flames.

00:20:22.306 --> 00:20:27.853
And I ordered Yu Lan to get rid
of the biggest cancer of all...

00:20:27.853 --> 00:20:30.397
the one that caused your downfall.

00:20:30.397 --> 00:20:31.481
Cancer?

00:20:31.481 --> 00:20:33.775
The woman, Kashim.

00:20:33.775 --> 00:20:36.111
Haven't you heard yet?

00:20:36.111 --> 00:20:38.614
I've heard every single word of it.

00:20:38.614 --> 00:20:42.451
Her body was mangled,
still wearing her cute school uniform.

00:20:42.451 --> 00:20:45.454
I heard she was pretty tough though,
and she didn't beg for her life.

00:20:45.454 --> 00:20:48.582
Her last words were "I'm sorry."

00:20:48.582 --> 00:20:50.542
I wonder who they were meant for?

00:20:50.542 --> 00:20:52.377
It brings tears to my eyes!

00:20:52.377 --> 00:20:53.879
Y-You're lying!

00:20:53.879 --> 00:20:56.173
It's true!

00:20:56.173 --> 00:21:01.011
I wanted to show you a picture of her body
so I could see the despair on your face,

00:21:01.011 --> 00:21:03.680
but I think I'm going to resist.

00:21:03.680 --> 00:21:05.015
'Cause you know what,

00:21:05.015 --> 00:21:08.810
the damage is written
all over your face, Kashim!

00:21:10.312 --> 00:21:13.690
My woman in Tokyo!

00:21:13.690 --> 00:21:15.859
I'm already too late!

00:21:15.859 --> 00:21:21.657
Aww, poor Kaname-<i>chan</i>!
She was such a nice girl, too!

00:21:21.657 --> 00:21:23.033
Gauron!

00:21:23.033 --> 00:21:25.077
That's right, I killed her.

00:21:25.077 --> 00:21:29.581
Now hate me. Go on, hate me, Kashim!

00:22:27.764 --> 00:22:33.312
<i>Kitto kimi wa kyou no hi mo</i>

00:22:33.312 --> 00:22:39.193
<i>Massugu ashita wo miteru</i>

00:22:39.193 --> 00:22:44.907
<i>Kaze ga fuku ano oka ni saita</i>

00:22:44.907 --> 00:22:51.663
<i>himawari no you ni</i>

00:22:53.582 --> 00:22:59.505
<i>Donna ni tooku hanareteite mo</i>

00:22:59.505 --> 00:23:05.511
<i>Kono utagoe ga kimi ni todoku you ni</i>

00:23:05.511 --> 00:23:11.558
<i>Namida ga zutto tomaranai yoru</i>

00:23:11.558 --> 00:23:17.898
<i>Kimi no mado wo terasu tsuki ni naritai</i>

00:23:17.898 --> 00:23:25.948
<i>Mata kanarazu aeru to</i>

00:23:28.283 --> 00:23:31.870
<i>Sou omou kara</i>

00:23:45.175 --> 00:23:45.676
"Next Episode"

00:23:45.676 --> 00:23:46.677
<i>Gauron.</i>

00:23:46.677 --> 00:23:50.180
<i>My old enemy was the only one</i>
<i>who saw completely through me.</i>

00:23:50.180 --> 00:23:54.643
<i>The devil beckons, and the</i>
<i>final calculated curse surfaces.</i>

00:23:54.643 --> 00:23:58.355
<i>Next time, the final episode:</i>
<i>"The Continuing Day by Day"</i>

00:23:58.355 --> 00:24:00.774
<i>Only one thing can crush despair:</i>

00:24:00.774 --> 00:24:04.715
<i>That single fierce blow.</i>
